WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.117 --> 00:00:01.567
(audience cheers)
- I love these pants.

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:04.170
Okay. So, and joining us remotely,

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.803
give it up for Brendan Fraser!

00:00:05.803 --> 00:00:07.153
(audience cheers)

00:00:07.153 --> 00:00:09.736
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.942 --> 00:00:14.055
What's up?

00:00:14.055 --> 00:00:14.888
- [Brendan] Hi, Kelly.

00:00:14.888 --> 00:00:17.040
- I know. He's here with us in spirit.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:17.873
There you are.

00:00:17.873 --> 00:00:18.750
Hi!

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:19.732
- Hi.

00:00:19.732 --> 00:00:21.000
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:21.833
- What's up, Sadie?

00:00:21.833 --> 00:00:22.710
Welcome to the show.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:23.910
- Oh, thank you for having me.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:25.260
- No, I'm very excited.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:26.190
A fellow Texas girl, too.

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.510
You're originally from Texas, right?

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:28.343
- Yes.
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:00:28.343 --> 00:00:29.520
I was born in Brenham, Texas.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.110
- I actually know where that is.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:33.148
Yeah, bunch of small
towns no one's heard of.

00:00:33.148 --> 00:00:34.620
Texas.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.090
So, Sadie, are you going to get

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.370
to spend the holidays with your family,

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:39.540
or are you going back
home or where do you go?

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.420
- Yeah, I'm gonna be with my family.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.570
And we have some very
exciting holiday traditions.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.610
- [Kelly] Wait, what are they?

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.230
- Christmas Eve karaoke is big.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.271
- [Kelly] Yes!

00:00:50.271 --> 00:00:52.740
- And then also we do a
cookie decorating competition,

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.930
and it's gets very competitive.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:56.220
- I love your family.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:57.930
- [Sadie] Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:57.930 --> 00:00:59.670
- Now, does this end

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:01.140
poorly sometimes?

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.130
- Oh, yeah.
- Okay. (laughs)

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:04.950
- A few tears have been
shed in past years.

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.120
- My family is competitive, too.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:07.837
My favorite part is my mother's like,

00:01:07.837 --> 00:01:08.730
"You and your sister,

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:09.690
y'all are so competitive."

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:12.630
and we're like, "You're like
the queen of competitive."

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:15.450
She's like, she throws
shade better than anyone,

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.100
and like, you don't even
know what's happening.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.330
Are you competitive?

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.040
Do you play games with
your family, Brendan?

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:21.672
- Full contact karaoke.

00:01:21.672 --> 00:01:23.457
(everyone laughs)

00:01:23.457 --> 00:01:25.483
- (sings) Should I stay
or should I go now?

00:01:25.483 --> 00:01:26.563
(imitates crashing noise)

00:01:26.563 --> 00:01:28.146
(everyone laughs)

00:01:28.146 --> 00:01:29.070
- Okay. You just upped karaoke in general.

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.450
I love your version.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:31.283
Well, to both of you,

00:01:31.283 --> 00:01:33.960
do you remember the coolest
gift you ever received?

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.340
Like, when you were little?

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:36.985
- Probably an American Girl Doll.

00:01:36.985 --> 00:01:38.422
- Oh my god, you're so young. (laughs)

00:01:38.422 --> 00:01:39.255
- They were huge when I was little.

00:01:39.255 --> 00:01:40.149
It was very-

00:01:40.149 --> 00:01:41.100
It was very special.
- Those weren't even around

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.750
when I was a kid.

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:43.590
That's amazing!

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:44.460
Do you remember which one?

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:46.350
My daughter loves the American Girl Dolls.

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:47.940
- Oh, Kit. Kit Kittredge.
- Oh, Kit, yeah.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:48.773
Love it.

00:01:48.773 --> 00:01:49.980
All right, all right.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:50.813
What about you Brendan?

00:01:50.813 --> 00:01:52.800
When you were little, what was
one of your favorite gifts?

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.047
- Only doll I got was a G.I. Joe.

00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:56.430
- (sings) G.I. Joe.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:57.630
I remember those, yeah.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.255
- He came with a parachute
built into his back.

00:02:00.255 --> 00:02:02.070
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:05.670
- I threw him off the balcony
from the second floor,

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:08.910
and he got stuck in a tree
until the next spring.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:10.818
He just kind of hung there.

00:02:10.818 --> 00:02:13.651
(everyone laughs)

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:16.950
- I love that.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:20.880
So he's still America's greatest hero.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:23.670
So you're originally from
Texas, you were saying,

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:26.910
so what's like, something
you miss from Texas?

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.170
- Oh,

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.220
probably "y'all."

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:31.620
No one says "y'all" where I live now.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.060
- [Kelly] Oh.
- And I miss that.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:34.020
- I can't drop it.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:34.890
I don't even know I'm doing it.

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.570
Especially when I drink, Sadie.

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.802
- Oh.
- [Kelly] Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:37.802 --> 00:02:38.635
(audience laughs)

00:02:38.635 --> 00:02:39.468
- Yeah, it's an issue.

00:02:39.468 --> 00:02:40.590
It's like I get the twang.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:43.350
Do you say like "light"
and "white", and like,

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:45.117
do you say "right" or "right"?

00:02:45.117 --> 00:02:47.910
- No, I mean, honestly
the Texas accent was

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:50.313
bullied out of me once
I moved to New York.

00:02:50.313 --> 00:02:51.960
- Okay.
- Around 10 years old.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.670
- Oh, okay.
- So I dropped it.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:55.230
- Yeah. You didn't want to
get beat up on the playground.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:56.063
- Sometimes when I get on the phone-

00:02:56.063 --> 00:02:56.896
Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:02:56.896 --> 00:02:57.729
All right, I gotcha.

00:02:57.729 --> 00:02:59.250
I just held on to mine

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:01.200
while getting beat up on the playground.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.790
So, what do you think the most

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.162
Texas thing about you is though?

00:03:04.162 --> 00:03:05.340
- I'm not sure.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.540
Probably the y'all thing.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:07.373
- [Kelly] Probably the, y'all?

00:03:07.373 --> 00:03:09.570
I really shed a lot of, a lot of my-

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:11.430
- I'm gonna put it back in there.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:12.263
What?
- Yeah.

00:03:12.263 --> 00:03:13.477
I'm very sad right now, Sadie.

00:03:13.477 --> 00:03:14.310
- You can help me.

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:15.270
- Okay. Yeah.

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:17.065
Whatever New Yorkers, we're cool.

00:03:17.065 --> 00:03:17.898
(laughs)

00:03:17.898 --> 00:03:18.731
Wait, so Brendan,

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:21.750
did you get to meet Sadie's family ever?

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:22.583
- I did.

00:03:22.583 --> 00:03:23.416
- Yeah?

00:03:23.416 --> 00:03:25.470
- At the premiere the other
night at Lincoln Center.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:28.248
Did you know that she has 93 siblings?

00:03:28.248 --> 00:03:30.600
(everyone laughs)

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.640
- Just four. I'm one of five.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:33.473
- That's a lot though.

00:03:33.473 --> 00:03:34.306
- Yeah.

00:03:34.306 --> 00:03:36.810
- Yeah.
- But they were all there.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:37.830
- [Kelly] That's exciting!

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:38.910
- Yeah. Real deep.

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:40.920
- Yeah. Were they, did you like,

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.707
watch them watching the
premiere like, the movie?

00:03:43.707 --> 00:03:45.630
- Yeah, I did. And a lot of them,

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:46.980
except for my mom were watching it

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:47.813
for the first time.

00:03:47.813 --> 00:03:50.367
It's definitely a difficult
movie to watch with your family.

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:51.200
- [Kelly] Yeah, it's intense.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.880
- Especially my dad, and
I was really excited for

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.140
the two of them to meet,

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:56.790
'cause it's a father-daughter story,

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.170
so it's a weird one to
watch with your own dad.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.730
- You have a very different relationship

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:00.900
with your father hopefully than-

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:01.733
- Yes. Yes.

00:04:01.733 --> 00:04:02.566
Very...yeah.
- Okay. (laughs)

00:04:02.566 --> 00:04:03.690
- [Kelly] I was like, if
you've seen "The Whale"-

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:05.640
- I'm never, I'm never that mean to him.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:06.570
- [Kelly] Yeah. (laughs)

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:08.190
- Your dad's a football coach.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:09.540
He doesn't take trouble

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:11.160
from anyone, I get the feeling.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:11.993
- Yeah.

00:04:11.993 --> 00:04:12.826
- Oh my gosh, wait, you're like,

00:04:12.826 --> 00:04:13.768
full on "Friday Night Lights".

00:04:13.768 --> 00:04:15.060
- Oh, full on.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.200
- Oh, that's amazing.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.033
- Yeah.

00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:18.390
- Football coaches in Texas are-

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:19.560
- It's intense.
It's a storm.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.150
- In high school football, too.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:23.010
- Yep.
The culture surrounding it.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.810
- They don't think they're in high school,

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:25.740
they think they're playing pro.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:26.573
- No no no.

00:04:26.573 --> 00:04:27.420
The stakes are, they are so high.

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:28.770
- Yep. Yep.

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:30.031
That's how it is.

00:04:30.031 --> 00:04:32.730
I remember being in the
stands in high school going,

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:35.370
no one's winning the
Super Bowl here. (laughs)

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.982
- But they might as well,
like it might as well

00:04:36.982 --> 00:04:37.815
have been the Super Bowl.

00:04:37.815 --> 00:04:38.648
- It is. I know.

00:04:38.648 --> 00:04:39.481
Not downplaying it.

00:04:39.481 --> 00:04:41.970
Just, they're very passionate
people about football.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:44.520
So Brendan, had you seen Stranger Things

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:45.726
before you met on the movie?

00:04:45.726 --> 00:04:46.559
- Yes, I have.

00:04:46.559 --> 00:04:48.780
I saw the first season in its entirety.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:51.390
I loved it 'cause I grew up
playing Dungeons and Dragons,

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:55.020
and the whole ensemble of
Stranger Things reminded me

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:57.300
of the crew that I used
to run around with when

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:01.173
I lived in Seattle, Washington
in the late seventies.

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:03.420
So it was nostalgia for me.

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:04.680
I loved it.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.530
And then, after we finished "The Whale",

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:09.660
a certain Sadie Sink went on

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:13.230
to stare down a really scary monster

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:14.512
called Vecna.

00:05:14.512 --> 00:05:15.780
(laughs)

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:19.230
And I know that's because

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:20.850
she had just come

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:21.940
from playing

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:24.990
Charlie's daughter

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:27.090
who has a great deal of

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.570
finely focused

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:31.800
anger issues with her father.

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:34.320
So I think Sadie
definitely carried her work

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:36.300
from one project into the other,

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:39.180
'cause that Vecna guy ran with
his tail between his legs.

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:40.710
And I know why, and it's not just

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:42.690
because her dad is a football coach

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:46.200
and has a handshake like a stone mason.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.495
I know, 'cause this hand still hurts.

00:05:48.495 --> 00:05:49.560
(everyone laughs)

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:51.030
- We're just trying to show our strength.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:52.890
It's a power struggle.

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:54.780
So Brendan, we have to
talk about "The Whale".

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:56.130
Explain what it's about to everybody.

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:58.020
It's a very intense movie.

00:05:58.020 --> 00:05:59.910
- Charlie's a man who's been living alone

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:02.310
in his two bedroom
apartment in northern Idaho.

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:03.510
He has certain life regrets

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:05.190
for choices that he's made

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:06.903
that led to him,

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:08.993
well,

00:06:08.993 --> 00:06:10.500
his family fell apart.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:13.380
He had fallen in love
while he was married,

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:18.030
and he started a new life
and left his daughter behind.

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:21.480
And he has clearly certain regrets,

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:24.900
and he has been harming
himself sadly by overeating.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.073
And his health isn't,

00:06:28.131 --> 00:06:28.964
is severe.

00:06:28.964 --> 00:06:31.980
And he has five days really to see

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:33.990
if he can reconnect with his daughter.

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:35.230
It's a quest for

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:37.823
redemption.

00:06:37.823 --> 00:06:38.656
- Redemption, yeah.

00:06:38.656 --> 00:06:39.489
- As the story goes.

00:06:39.489 --> 00:06:40.680
That's the film.

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:44.640
It was directed by Darren Aronofsky

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:46.620
who brought us "Black Swan"

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:47.967
and "The Wrestler",

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:51.480
and it was a thrill to work with

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:53.730
a world-class filmmaker like Darren.

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:54.563
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:54.563 --> 00:06:55.510
- [Brendan] He really knows
how to call the shots.

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:58.170
- Yeah, and y'all do an incredible job.

00:06:58.170 --> 00:07:00.360
Like, I mean you did so well.

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:03.030
You've been getting
standing ovations, like,

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:04.650
and, you know, people are just-

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:07.680
it's a very impressive
film to won. I just-

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:09.150
Do you take that home with you?

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:10.590
Like, that's the hardest thing.

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:11.850
Like even if I'm writing a song,

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:12.810
and it's like depressing,

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:14.160
and I'm getting through something,

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.900
I have to like get it out and let it go.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:17.820
But every day you had to come back

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:19.770
and go back to these scenes
that were so intense.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.990
Is that hard to shake when you go home?

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:23.310
- What do you think Sadie?

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:25.230
I mean we had three weeks to rehearse it,

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:26.310
which was really helpful.

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:29.280
So we really knew the
lives of these characters.

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:31.800
But I think if we took it home

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:35.516
it might have just been,
in my case, because I was

00:07:35.516 --> 00:07:39.480
costumed in apparatus that

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:42.570
increased Charlie's body size,

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:44.640
that when I took it
off, I felt a little bit

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:47.550
weak-kneed or wobbly just because of,

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:51.810
I think, that new muscles
were activated in my own body,

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:54.750
and somehow it gave me
a sense of appreciation

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:56.490
for those who live with obesity

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:58.320
in a way that I was not expecting.

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:00.750
- Absolutely. I can't imagine
having to wear that every day.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:03.713
So how did putting on the
300 pound prosthetic suit

00:08:03.713 --> 00:08:05.970
change the way you look at the world?

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:08.820
- Well, it gave me a
stronger sense of empathy

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:11.940
for those who live with the disease.

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:14.370
And I know that

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:16.097
our work with the Obesity Action Coalition

00:08:16.097 --> 00:08:18.090
was very helpful

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:21.390
to advise us about the film.

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:25.320
And overall, their mission
statement is to end bias

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:28.740
against those who carry
extra weight on their body.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:32.820
And I think that it gave me a strong sense

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:37.050
of obligation to portray
this character Charlie

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:41.493
with the dignity and
empathy that he deserves.

